1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,649
You've spent years arguing about offside, with

2
00:00:02,461 --> 00:00:04,142
four rules that don't exist.

3
00:00:04,994 --> 00:00:05,750
Myth one:

4
00:00:05,735 --> 00:00:07,752
he was level, so he's offside.

5
00:00:08,347 --> 00:00:09,137
False.

6
00:00:09,736 --> 00:00:12,297
Level with the second-last opponent is onside.

7
00:00:13,170 --> 00:00:13,972
Myth two:

8
00:00:13,980 --> 00:00:15,627
his arm was past the defender.

9
00:00:16,222 --> 00:00:17,116
Still no.

10
00:00:17,715 --> 00:00:19,385
Hands and arms never count:

11
00:00:19,393 --> 00:00:21,271
only head, body and feet.

12
00:00:22,138 --> 00:00:22,917
Myth three:

13
00:00:22,925 --> 00:00:24,410
he was all alone when he got

14
00:00:24,221 --> 00:00:24,873
the ball.

15
00:00:25,468 --> 00:00:26,304
So what?

16
00:00:26,903 --> 00:00:29,013
The snapshot is taken when his team-mate

17
00:00:28,824 --> 00:00:30,945
plays the ball, not when it arrives.

18
00:00:31,802 --> 00:00:32,511
Myth four:

19
00:00:32,485 --> 00:00:34,676
standing in an offside position is already

20
00:00:34,487 --> 00:00:35,324
an offence.

21
00:00:35,919 --> 00:00:36,570
No.

22
00:00:37,169 --> 00:00:38,931
Position alone is never punished:

23
00:00:38,928 --> 00:00:40,586
he has to get involved in play.

24
00:00:41,466 --> 00:00:42,395
And a bonus:

25
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:43,761
if the ball comes to you straight

26
00:00:43,572 --> 00:00:45,231
from a throw-in, a goal kick or

27
00:00:45,042 --> 00:00:46,967
a corner, there's no offside.

28
00:00:47,842 --> 00:00:49,604
Offside isn't just where you are.

29
00:00:50,199 --> 00:00:52,170
It's when, with what, and what you

30
00:00:51,982 --> 00:00:52,564
do.

31
00:00:53,426 --> 00:00:54,945
Save it, and share it with the

32
00:00:54,757 --> 00:00:56,751
friend who calls everything offside from the

33
00:00:56,563 --> 00:00:57,237
sofa.

